{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1167765-dream-manipulation-olympics","id":1167765,"title":"Dream Manipulation Olympics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-14T13:58:21-08:00","id":1167765,"title":"Dream Manipulation Olympics","content":"Inspired by the Changeling KS, I've been thinking about which splats have the...not necessarily &quot;best&quot; powers when it comes to manipulating a given mortal's dreams, but maybe the &quot;broadest&quot;? And how to operationalize different methods in a crossover game. (I'm assuming this is too niche to be covered in depth in the Contagion Chronicle.)<br /> <br /> <b>Beasts </b>are of course living nightmares, but they actually seem to have the least granular control over dreams; Nightmares and Lair Traits work mainly as a gestalt. They do, however, have the ability to bring the Primordial Dream into the material world via Lair Traits, and their Horror gives them a very powerful Dream Form.<br /> <br /> <b>Changelings </b>can inherently use dreamweaving like Hedgespinning, and can physically enter a Bastion through the Gate of Horn. The main limit seems to be the Composure penalty imposed by the dreamer, and the need to generate large numbers of successes (probably via Teamwork) to achieve major changes, but they can still achieve a lot with just subtle shifts.<br /> <br /> <b>The Merrick Institute </b>have the dream shaping merits from <i>Tooth and Nail, </i>which actually seem to be on a par with Changeling oneiromancy <i>if </i>you have the Experience to buy all those dots. They also don't seem to take a Composure penalty for dream shaping actions the way Changelings do, and they can be aided by waking cell members (again using merits from TnN.)<br /> <br /> <b>Mages </b>using the Arcanum of Mind can probably do the most anything a Changeling could do, but I admit this is the line I have the least experience with so I'm not sure how the nitty-gritty stacks up.<br /> <br /> Which other splats can interact with dreams?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T10:31:34-08:00","id":1168219,"title":"","content":"There is a bloodline of the Mekhet clan called the Alucinor; they have a custom discipline called Insomnium that lets them mess around with dreams. The Mekhet can also take a merit that gives them prophetic dreams, but I'm not sure you're counting that for this. Otherwise, the Nightmare and Auspex disciplines might have some devotions for it.<br /> <br /> Werewolves can also get some minor dream interaction abilities from some of their gifts I believe; of course, I'm not particularly well versed in werewolf so I could be remembering things wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","user":"Ever Professional","date":". 12-16-2017, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T12:20:29-08:00","id":1168232,"title":"","content":"I dunno how they actually stack up, but I feel like, thematically, Changelings and other Fae should be able to outdo the feats of any other supernatural with similar base stats, except a Mage either focusing most of their magical study on dreams or uncaring of Paradox. That's not to say a starting Changeling should be able to laugh off the attacks of an Elder Alucinor, but it should be hard to match the dreamshaping might of a high-Wyrd fae in a fair contest no matter who you are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T13:50:04-08:00","id":1168244,"title":"","content":"There was also a Dreamborn Lineage for Prometheans in 1e, which was represented as Extempore in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T02:34:29-08:00","id":1168339,"title":"","content":"<br /> Now, other than the Alucinor bloodline, there's also a devotion called Wet Dreams that, well, yeah; its exactly what you'd expect from a Majesty/Nightmare devotion. There's also the prophetic Mehket dream merit thing.<br /> <br /> Werewolf Cahalith get prophetic dreams and can cause some nightmares with their Auspice Gifts.<br /> <br /> Mind mages have the spell Dream Reaching; this lets you either shape and watch a dream from the outside, or enter into the dream and use Astral Realm rules to do stuff while inside.<br /> <br /> As LL said, there's the dreamborn promethean (kind of like how the real world describes tulpa)<br /> <br /> Changelings are the undisputed masters of dream stuff.<br /> <br /> Hunters have had a few prophetic dreams and nightmare causing things, much like werewolves, but not much otherwise.<br /> <br /> I don't remember anything relating dreams to Sin-Eaters and Mummies; a search on codcodex revealed nothing for sin eaters, while there's the Dream of the Dead Gods Utterance, which is just more inflicting dreams and not being in them.<br /> <br /> Demons could create visions and dreams using the Muse embed.<br /> <br /> Beasts do the whole Astral thing, which has an odd relationship with actual dreams. I feel like the Dreaming Roads are the border between the Hedge and Astral, and you can enter into a dream from either side to affect things. So, you can open a primordial pathway into someone's dreams similar to how you can open a pathway into the onerios. Mage already does astral rules in dreams, so I imagine that Beasts can do the same. .... We really need more Astral stuff for Beast.<br /> <br /> We know nothing of Deviants and dreams.<br /> <br /> <br /> The long and short of it seems to be that, other than 'lings, beasts and mages, most people can do prophetic dreams or inflict a nightmare type situation. Mages get to do anything, beasts can show up anywhere and use their Lair, Atavisms and Nightmares to do some scultping, but for the most part this is where changelings get the full breadth of abiltiles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 12-17-2017, 06:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}